## Context

Seven figures appear in `slides/manuscript/main.md`. Their axis labels,
titles, and figure captions were written as technical documentation and
reviewed in conversation 2026-05-25. Three issues recur:

1. **Language mix** — French labels inside English figures (fig_direct_p1_base,
   fig_direct_cost_quality).
2. **Opaque jargon** — "F1 score", "active parameters", "Source 2",
   "inventory rows", "arm" — unexplained for a non-specialist reader.
3. **Missing or docstring-style titles** — capability_dag axis labels say
   "Feature i (row)" / "Feature j (column)"; fig_exp2_arms_comparison
   panel ylabels use internal variable names.

Scope: the seven manuscript figures only (slides-only figures excluded as
out of scope for the conference talk).

## Figures and proposed changes

### fig_direct_p1_base  (`plot_method_convergence.py`)
- Add figure title (currently none)
- xlabel: replace FR "Nombre de centrales bien identifiées" → EN
  "Power plants identified (each dot = one plant)"
- Proposed title: "Which models recall Vietnam's 163 thermal power plants
  from memory?"

### fig_direct_cost_quality  (`plot_cost_quality.py`)
- ylabel: replace FR "Nombre de centrales bien identifiées"
  → "Power plants correctly identified (out of 163)"
- suptitle: replace "Experiment 1 baseline (no web search)"
  → "More expensive models don't reliably produce better inventories"
- Confirm panel labels use family names, not product names

### fig_spider_exp1_families  (spider / radar, family quality profiles)
- Add instructional subtitle explaining radar geometry
- Spoke labels: "Provenance" → "Source citation";
  "Temporality" → "Date accuracy"

### fig_capability_timeline  (`plot_capability_timeline.py`)
- Add title: "From chatbots to multi-agent systems: the AI capability
  frontier (2022–2025)"
- Add subtitle explaining 'TBD' markers

### fig_capability_dag  (`plot_capability_dag.py`)
- xlabel: replace "Feature j (column)" → "Shipped later →"
- ylabel: replace "Feature i (row)" → "Shipped earlier →"
- Title: replace docstring → "AI labs follow a consistent
  capability build-up order"

### fig_exp2_arms_comparison  (`plot_exp2_arms_comparison.py`)
- Panel A ylabel: "inventory_rows" → "Power plants enumerated"
- Panel B ylabel: "narrative_chars" → "Report length (thousands of characters)"
- Panel C ylabel: "cost_usd" → "Cost per run (USD)"
- suptitle: remove "arm" vocabulary; keep N=5 count

### fig_exp2_coverage_certainty  (`plot_exp2_coverage_certainty.py`)
- ylabel: "Rows with Source 2 (corroboration)"
  → "Entries with two independent sources"
- xlabel: "Inventory rows (coverage)" → "Power plants enumerated"
- Add title: "Longer inventories tend to be better sourced"

## Exit criteria

- [ ] All French labels replaced with English equivalents
- [ ] fig_capability_dag axis labels are human-readable
- [ ] fig_exp2_arms_comparison panel ylabels use plain English
- [ ] fig_exp2_coverage_certainty "Source 2" replaced
- [ ] fig_capability_timeline and fig_direct_p1_base have titles
- [ ] `make check-fast` passes
- [ ] Figures regenerate without error
